<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Vladislav</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1018</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ivan Vladislav of Bulgaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Vladislav (died 1018) was the last tsar of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>, ruling from 1015 to 1018. A nephew of Samuel, whose life had been spared at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavril-radomir">Gavril Radomir</a>'s request when his father Aron was killed, he seized the throne by murdering Gavril Radomir. He continued the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> but was killed in 1018 while besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Dyrrhachium</a>, after which the Bulgarian nobility and his widow Maria surrendered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-vladislav.jpg" alt="Ivan Vladislav" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Madrid Skylitzes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IvanVladislav.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
